WEBVTT

00:03.700 --> 00:08.103
Every cite the planner writes carries evidence tokens the gate

00:08.203 --> 00:11.807
must find in the cited lines. Its budget grows with

00:11.907 --> 00:14.640
the cite: room for two tokens per line.

00:17.250 --> 00:22.232
Proportional must not mean unbounded. Two bounds shape the budget: a

00:22.332 --> 00:25.670
floor for short cites and a cap for long ones.

00:25.783 --> 00:29.679
A one-line cite still gets room for five tokens: a

00:29.779 --> 00:34.155
FLOOR on the budget, so short cites keep their coverage.

00:34.266 --> 00:39.614
And a long cite stops at a CAP of twenty-four, so it stays readable.

00:43.916 --> 00:47.652
The budget is a ceiling, not a promise. A planned

00:47.752 --> 00:52.192
cite that cannot yield real proof never reaches the video.

00:52.300 --> 00:55.664
Fewer than two tokens, or none of them strong, and

00:55.764 --> 00:59.544
the planner drops the whole beat instead of shipping it.
